{"actions":[{"actionCode":null,"actionDate":"2026-03-18","source":"Senate","text":"Committee on Veterans' Affairs. Ordered to be reported with an amendment in the nature of a substitute favorably.","type":"Committee"},{"actionCode":null,"actionDate":"2025-05-13","source":"Senate","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Veterans' Affairs.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"10000","actionDate":"2025-05-13","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in Senate","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/1726","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"H001042","fullName":"Sen. Hirono, Mazie K. [D-HI]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-07-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"HI"},{"bioguideId":"S001181","fullName":"Sen. Shaheen, Jeanne [D-NH]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NH"},{"bioguideId":"B001299","fullName":"Sen. Banks, Jim [R-IN]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-10","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"},{"bioguideId":"B001243","fullName":"Sen. Blackburn, Marsha [R-TN]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-16","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TN"},{"bioguideId":"B001277","fullName":"Sen. Blumenthal, Richard [D-CT]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-02-02","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CT"},{"bioguideId":"K000383","fullName":"Sen. King, Angus S., Jr. [I-ME]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"I","sponsorshipDate":"2026-02-25","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"ME"},{"bioguideId":"R000605","fullName":"Sen. Rounds, Mike [R-SD]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-03-04","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"SD"},{"bioguideId":"S001208","fullName":"Sen. Slotkin, Elissa [D-MI]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-22","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MI"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T06:33:50+00:00","id":"s1726-119","introducedDate":"2025-05-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-03-18","text":"Committee on Veterans' Affairs. Ordered to be reported with an amendment in the nature of a substitute favorably."},"laws":[],"number":"1726","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Armed Forces and National Security","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"T000278","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Tuberville, Tommy [R-AL]","party":"R","state":"AL"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-05-13","actionDesc":"Introduced in Senate","text":"<p><strong>Automotive Support Services to Improve Safe Transportation Act of 2025 or the ASSIST Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill expands the definition of <em>medical services</em> for purposes of veterans’ benefits to include additional medically necessary automobile&nbsp;adaptations. Under the bill, the Department of Veterans Affairs may provide funding for the following medically necessary automobile adaptations for driver or passenger use:&nbsp;ramp and kneeling systems, lowered floors, occupied and unoccupied mobility lifts, ingress or egress accessibility modifications, and adapted seating.&nbsp;</p><p>The bill also extends the limitation on pension amounts for certain hospitalized or institutionalized veterans through September 30, 2032.</p>","updateDate":"2025-08-12T16:25:19Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"ASSIST Act of 2025","type":"s","updateDate":"2026-04-23T11:03:25Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-04-23T11:03:25Z"}
